--------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The whole repository is Apache-2.0: the engine (prometheus.py), the nemesis
security gate, Prometheus Studio, the prometheus CLI/TUI, the VS Code
extension and the prometheus_plugin adapters.

Earlier revisions licensed the client packages (the CLI, the VS Code
extension and the prometheus_plugin adapters) under MIT. They were
relicensed to Apache-2.0 on 2026-10-01, before the first public release, so
that one licence governs the project and the attribution requirement in
Section 4(d) reaches every part of it. MIT carries no equivalent NOTICE
obligation; that difference is the reason for the change.

Each package's own `license` field remains the source of truth for that
package, and all eleven of them now read Apache-2.0.

One deliberate exception, which is not part of the product:
`studio/examples/extensions/csv-lens/` is a REFERENCE FIXTURE demonstrating what a
third-party Studio extension looks like, and it carries its own MIT licence
precisely to show that an external extension brings its own terms. It ships no
code that PROMETHEUS depends on.

Third-party components redistributed with this software are listed, with
their own licences and attribution requirements, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
Those obligations are independent of this file and are not modified by it.
